From 478d23107dae34ba7423cb0439093918e7417a81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 19:46:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Refuse hopeless lip-sync sources and make the model
 swappable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two guards around the lip_sync engine.

RESOLUTION FLOOR. Upscaling rescues a 480p upload; it cannot rescue a
144p one, because there is no mouth detail to enlarge. Sources below
MIN_USABLE_HEIGHT are now refused with a message naming the height,
before the model is called — the job fails into the existing refund
path having spent nothing on Replicate. The check reuses the probe
the source-preparation pass already performs, so it costs no extra
work. It deliberately runs in the runner rather than the route: the
route would have to load the whole upload a second time to see the
resolution, and the refund path already makes the user whole.

MODEL OVERRIDE. The lip-sync model was pinned at its call site, which
made "is LatentSync the ceiling or the bug?" a question only a deploy
could answer. generateLipSyncWithReplicate now takes an optional model
reference, resolved from a new video_gen_settings.lip_sync_model
column, then the LIPSYNC_MODEL environment variable, then the pinned
default — the same precedence the stored API credentials already use.
Job rows record the model that actually ran.

Lip sync stays out of VideoGenSelection on purpose: its input contract
is video + audio rather than a prompt, so it is not one of the
providers that selection switches between, and keeping it separate
leaves the admin route, the API spec and the generated clients
untouched. There is no admin card for it yet — set the column or the
env var to run a comparison.

Requires: pnpm --filter @workspace/db run push

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
